    {
      "id": "r20261120-a02",
      "title": "The History of Instant Noodles",
      "level": "Menengah",
      "min": 3,
      "body": [
        "Instant noodles were invented in Japan in 1958 by a man named Momofuku Ando. After the war, food was scarce, and he wanted to make something cheap, tasty, and easy to store. His first flavor was chicken.",
        "The idea spread quickly. In 1971, Ando's company put noodles in a cup, so people only needed hot water. Today, people around the world eat about 100 billion servings of instant noodles every year. Indonesia is one of the biggest markets, with flavors like rendang and soto.",
        "Instant noodles are convenient, but doctors warn that they should not replace real meals. They are high in salt and low in vitamins. The healthiest way to enjoy them is simple: add an egg, some vegetables, and use only half the seasoning."
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "invented": "ditemukan",
